      "deck_title": "Workplace Security",
      "group": "Workplace & Login Security",
      "slide_tag": null,
      "eyebrow": "Everyday Defence",
      "h1": "YOUR DESK IS PART OF THE PERIMETER",
      "section_lead": [
        "Four things worth noticing at any desk \u2014 two risks, two good habits. Plus what should happen the moment you walk away."
      ],
      "cards": [
        {
          "tag": "h4",
          "heading": "Password on a Sticky Note Risk",
          "body": "Never leave passwords written where others can see them. Use a password manager instead."
        },
        {
          "tag": "h4",
          "heading": "Locked Screen Good Practice",
          "body": "Lock your screen (Win+L / Cmd+Ctrl+Q) every time you leave, even for a moment."
        },
        {
          "tag": "h4",
          "heading": "Unknown USB Drive Risk",
          "body": "Never plug in a USB stick you don't own or haven't checked with IT. It can install harmful software silently the moment you plug it in."
        },
        {
          "tag": "h4",
          "heading": "Badge Worn Visibly Good Practice",
          "body": "Keep your badge visible, and don't let anyone follow you through a secure door."
        },
        {
          "tag": "h4",
          "heading": "What Should Happen When You Walk Away",
          "body": "After a short idle period, the screen should lock automatically \u2014 no action needed from you. If it doesn't, lock it yourself before you go."
        }
      ],
